WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.125
In the previous module, we

2
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:23.640
introduced you to several trades

3
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.420
designed to be of use in
either up or down markets.

4
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.130
In this module, we'll explore

5
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.990
a couple of strategies
that may be used

6
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.520
by option traders to take

7
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.485
advantage of a low
in the markets.

8
00:00:34.485 --> 00:00:36.870
By low, I'm referring to a period

9
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.200
of relatively small
movements in the price

10
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.240
of an underlying asset where

11
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.195
volatility is
expected to diminish.

12
00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:46.400
Once again, we'll walk
you through examples of

13
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.530
how each strategy works
and then show you

14
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.350
a practical application
of how such trades may be

15
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.625
created using IBKR's
Trader Workstation.

16
00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:56.600
While we're talking
specifically about

17
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.030
strategies designed
for neutral markets,

18
00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.160
don't forget that the
opposite side of each

19
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.380
trade infers higher volatility,

20
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.720
which would appeal to
option traders looking for

21
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.715
larger price movements or

22
00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:11.950
upward shifts in
volatility. Let's begin.